spoz2 0.1

# NOW: a tiny personal focus tool.  This file is the example SPOZ2 used
# to discover the language.  It describes two versions of NOW.

system now
  A personal focus tool.  A human keeps a list of things they could do;
  NOW is the one thing they are doing right now.  The point of the tool
  is to keep NOW honest: singular, current and owned by a person.

invariant one-active-now
  since 1.0
  A human may have only one active NOW item at any time.
  Starting a new NOW item ends the previous one.

invariant now-belongs-to-human
  since 1.0
  Every NOW item belongs to exactly one human.

invariant now-expires-at-midnight
  since 1.1
  until 2.0
  An active NOW item is automatically ended at local midnight.
  Retired in 2.0 without replacement: people working across midnight
  hated it, and workspaces made it unnecessary.

invariant one-active-now
  since 2.0
  A human may have at most one active NOW item per workspace.
  Version 2.0 introduced workspaces (for example "work" and "home").
  Within a single workspace the 1.0 rule still holds: starting a new
  NOW item in a workspace ends the previous one in that workspace.
